course: dictionary
lesson: 3155
title: Words that mean something is starting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Emergence is a noun, a name for the moment something comes out into view or starts to exist. Its root is emerge, which means to come out, and the ending -ence turns it into the name of that event.
explain: The first meaning is about things coming out. A butterfly makes its emergence from its chrysalis, and seedlings make their emergence from the soil. The second meaning is about ideas or groups becoming known. «In an ant colony, simple rules followed by each ant lead to clever group results with no ant knowing the plan; this is called emergence.» The clever pattern appears from simple rules, and nobody planned it.
explain: Read the words around emergence for clues. The phrase «the emergence of» often comes before a new thing, such as farming, cities or a new nation, and it tells you when that thing began. To check your meaning, swap in "coming out" or "starting" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Emergence means coming out from somewhere and becoming visible, or starting to exist or become known.
fact: «The emergence of» something tells you when it began, such as «the emergence of cities».
fact: A butterfly's emergence is the moment it comes out of its chrysalis.
fact: Emergence can also be a clever pattern that appears from simple rules, as in an ant colony where no ant knows the plan.
fact: «Emergence from» means coming out of something, such as seedlings emerging from soil.
exercise: A butterfly makes its emergence from the chrysalis. What does emergence mean here? | *Coming out and becoming visible | Falling asleep for the winter | Losing its colour | Flying away from home
exercise: «The emergence of farming» tells us about the past. What does this phrase show? | When farming ended | Where the farmers lived | *When farming began | How much farmers were paid
exercise: «In an ant colony, simple rules followed by each ant lead to clever group results with no ant knowing the plan; this is called emergence.» What is emergence in this sentence? | The end of the colony | Ants arguing about the plan | *A clever group result that appears from simple rules | One ant leading the whole colony
test: What does emergence mean in «the emergence of a new country»? | Leaving the country | Drawing a map of the country | Its ending | *Starting to exist or becoming known
test: Which word is the noun meaning coming out or starting to exist? | Emerged | Emerge | Emergent | *Emergence
exam: In «seedlings make their emergence from the soil», what does emergence mean? | *Coming up out of the soil and becoming visible | Digging a hole | Hiding under the soil | Being watered
